eatures: floor picker (◀ ▶ + name), the floor rendered with the REAL renderer (floor tiles, walls, elevators via render_comms's elevator drawing if reusable, zones/rooms outlines with labels, spawns as coloured diamonds by type, pickups, entry/exits, and PROPS animated live at their pixel grid), camera pan (drag with middle/space or right-drag) + wheel zoom (add a wheel event in input.rs if none) + FIT; grid + snap (10 units default, toggle); tools: SELECT/MOVE (drag; resize handles for rects), WALL, ROOM, ZONE, SPAWN (type cycle), PICKUP (weapon cycle), ENTRY, EXIT, PROP (a palette: family pages DATACENTER/… showing prop thumbnails via draw_prop, click to pick, click on map to place; R rotates 90°, [ ] resize, arrow keys nudge, Del deletes); an editable in-memory `EditableFloor` (owned Vecs; `from(&FloorDef)`, `to_json()` hand-written serializer producing the documented key order and round-tripping the scenario steps/exits/etc. verbatim — implement a tiny JSON writer; no serde, no crates); undo/redo (snapshot stack, 100); a small text-field widget for ids/labels (click to focus, type, Enter/Esc; use input keys) — keep it minimal (walls need none; zones/rooms/exits ids/labels do); a properties strip for the selection; validation line (ids unique, exits' `to` valid, refs used by scenario exist — reuse rules from the doc); SAVE → wasm→JS extern `vizSaveLevel(file, json)` (add to index.html mirroring `vizSaveProps`, PUT /levels/<file>.json with the same token flow, toast with \"now run: make gen-levels\"). Keep `?viz`'s other tabs untouched. Keyboard shortcuts listed on-screen.\n  4. Keep the fallback wasm LEVELS map (draw_viz_levels) as the FIT/overview if convenient or remove it — your call; don't leave dead code.\n\n  CONSTRAINTS: no new deps; opcode tables untouched (no new opcodes needed); CLAUDE.md updated (?viz LEVELS = native editor + SCENARIO (web) button; props in floors; format); localized lib.rs edits (dispatch + a few fields), all real code in src/editor*.rs; unit tests for the JSON writer round-trip (parse the generated JSON back with a tiny test parser or compare against gen_levels.py: run `python3 tools/gen_levels.py --check` after writing a floor via the editor's serializer to prove it's accepted) and for EditableFloor edits/undo.\n\n  VERIFY: `make verify` green (fmt, host+wasm clippy, tests, build, wasm, check-levels/props). `make build-wasm`; serve `python3 serve.py 8100` (port 8100 only, from the worktree root); headless Playwright (cd tests/e2e; chromium args --enable-unsafe-swiftshader --use-gl=angle --use-angle=swiftshader; LD_LIBRARY_PATH=\"$(find \"$PWD/tests/e2e/playwright-deps/libs\" -name '*.so*' -printf '%h\\n'|sort -u|paste -sd:)\"; clicks/keys HELD 150 ms). Screenshots to shots/editor_native_*.png (in the worktree's shots/, create it): the LEVELS tab with floor 11 rendered natively incl. placed props; the prop palette open; a prop being placed/rotated; a wall drawn + zone with label; the SAVE toast; and `?floor=1` gameplay showing the placed props under the action. Zero console errors. Report: format change, generator, in-game render, the editor's architecture (files, widget set, EditableFloor + JSON writer), keyboard map, screenshots, caveats, and the exact lib.rs regions you touched. Ping when done; stop the 8100 server."}]}
